      user whose card had more would otherwise assume editing threw it away.
    -->
    <string name="contacts_edit_preserves_note">Anything else your imported card holds is kept, even though it is not shown here.</string>

    <!--
      Platform import (Ph7). The three source rows are ordered by what they cost the user,
      and each supporting line says that cost plainly — the address-book row is the only one
      that asks for a permission, and it says so before it is tapped rather than letting the
      OS dialog be the first news of it.
    -->
    <string name="contacts_import_title">Import contacts</string>
    <string name="contacts_import_intro">Bring people in from this device. Nothing is sent anywhere — imported contacts live in your own Tenshu, like everything else.</string>
    <!-- The same thing in one line, for the FAB sheet row that opens the import sheet. -->
    <string name="contacts_import_intro_short">Bring people in from this device.</string>
    <string name="contacts_import_one_contact">Pick one person</string>
    <string name="contacts_import_one_contact_supporting">Choose a single contact. Tenshu never sees the rest of your address book.</string>
    <string name="contacts_import_file">Import a .vcf file</string>
    <string name="contacts_import_file_supporting">Any address book can export one.</string>
    <string name="contacts_import_address_book">Import your whole address book</string>
    <string name="contacts_import_address_book_supporting">Asks for permission to read your contacts.</string>
    <string name="contacts_import_working">Reading…</string>
    <!--
      Two strings rather than a plural resource, following drive-shared-ui: the project has
      no <plurals> in a composeResources catalogue and ADR 0016 defers the ICU one at n = 1.
    -->
    <string name="contacts_import_result_one">Imported 1 contact.</string>
    <string name="contacts_import_result_many">Imported %1$d contacts.</string>
    <string name="contacts_import_done">Done</string>
    <!--
      ⚠ D7. Import creates a new contact per card, always — recognising a duplicate is
      user-assisted merge (contacts_merge_*), never automatic. Said before the import, not
      after it, and it points at where the duplicates surface: the list's banner.
    -->
    <string name="contacts_import_no_merge_note">Everyone you import is added as a new contact, even if you already have them. Any possible duplicates then show up above your contact list, where you can review and combine them.</string>
    <string name="contacts_import_failed_permission">Tenshu could not read your contacts. Try "Import your whole address book", which asks for permission properly.</string>
    <string name="contacts_import_failed_unreadable">That could not be read.</string>
    <string name="contacts_import_failed_no_cards">No contacts were found there.</string>
    <string name="contacts_import_failed_nothing">Those contacts could not be saved.</string>

